# =====================================================================
# Credentials — never commit.
#
# The original working copy carried live Anthropic API keys in cell-local
# .env files (and one .env.identity-linked.bak). Those keys must be rotated
# externally before this repository is initialized; see README.md,
# "Environment and credentials".
# =====================================================================
.env
.env.*
*.env
# ...but the credential TEMPLATE is tracked deliberately.
# This negation must stay AFTER the .env.* rule above to take effect.
!.env.example

# =====================================================================
# Python caches (regenerated on demand; never authoritative)
# =====================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# =====================================================================
# Editor / IDE local state
#   .idea/ was present in study2_repeated_negotiation/ (PyCharm project state)
# =====================================================================
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# =====================================================================
# Local Claude Code state
#   negotiation_exp/.claude/settings.local.json held machine-local
#   tool permissions. Shared .claude config, if ever added, stays tracked.
#   The `**/` prefix is required: a pattern containing a slash is anchored
#   to this file's directory, so a bare `.claude/settings.local.json` would
#   match only at the repository root and miss the per-cell copies.
# =====================================================================
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# =====================================================================
# OS junk
# =====================================================================
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# =====================================================================
# Machine-specific / transient build artifacts
#   None of the following were present in the audited tree; listed to keep
#   them out if a future reader runs tooling inside the repository.
# =====================================================================
node_modules/
.vite/
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# =====================================================================
# NOT ignored, deliberately — these look like junk but are research record:
#   phase3_p3b_enforcement/runs/_to_delete/   historical test scratch (documented)
#   study2_repeated_negotiation/runs/_probe.txt, runs/pilot_stdout.log
#   study2_repeated_negotiation/runs/main_v2_1/DO_NOT_USE.md
#   study2_repeated_negotiation/runs/aborted_main_v2_1_credit/ABORTED.md
#   study3_pilot/runs/_sample_fake/           fabricated format examples
#   study3_pilot*/reading_log_template.md     referenced by run_pilot.py
# Do not add ignore rules for anything under a runs/ directory.
# =====================================================================
